\description{
tclustIC (where the last two letters stand for 'Information Criterion') computes the values of BIC (MIXMIX), ICL (MIXCLA) or CLA (CLACLA), for different values of k (number of groups) and different values of c (restriction factor), for a prespecified level of trimming. If Parallel Computing toolbox is installed, parfor is used to compute tclust for different values of c. In order to minimize randomness, given k, the same subsets are used for each value of c.
}
